{#-
  The YouTube note (SPEC §9.1, §15.1): once per page, at the end of every
  page with a video (layouts/problem.njk and layouts/start.njk), as a quiet
  note in smaller, slate-grey italic text. It says what pressing play does
  about YouTube's storage. Draft wording until HREC approval.

  It used to sit under each video; the project lead moved it to the end of
  the page on 2026-11-07 (SPEC §22), with the privacy officer to confirm
  (§21). So that pressing play stays an informed choice for screen-reader
  users, every play control names the note's sentences (id youtube-note-text,
  not the link) in aria-describedby (partials/video.njk): they hear the note
  with "Play video" although it is at the end of the page. A build test
  checks that each page with a video has the note exactly once.

    {% from "notices/video.njk" import youtubeNote %}
    {{ youtubeNote() }}
-#}
{%- macro youtubeNote() -%}
<p class="notice-text youtube-note"><span id="youtube-note-text">Pressing play on a video loads it from YouTube (Google). YouTube may then store cookies in your browser and collect information about what you watch.</span> <a href="/privacy/#cookies-and-browser-storage">More about this</a></p>
{%- endmacro -%}
